{{Term/Store|Heat||Series, BotW, TotK}},{{Exp Game|BotW, TotK}}<ref name="BotW Tips and Tricks"/><ref name="TotK Tips and Tricks"/> also known as '''Extreme Heat'''{{Exp Game|BotW}}<ref name="BotW Malena"/> and {{Term/Store|Desert Heat||HW, HWL, HWDE}},{{Exp Game|HW}}<ref name="HW Battle Log"/> is a recurring mechanic in {{TLoZ Series}}.{{Name Ref|HWL, HWDE}}

==Overview==
==={{BotW|-}}===
Heat occurs during the daytime in the [[Gerudo Desert]]. When the [[Temperature]] rises above 104°F, Link will experience one level of Heat and slowly take damage. When the Temperature rises above 122°F, as in [[Extremely Hot Zone]]s, he will experience two levels of Heat and take damage more quickly. Link can avoid taking damage from Heat by taking shelter within shade, submerging himself in a body of [[Water (Terrain)|Water]], equipping certain pieces of [[Armor]], consuming [[Chilly Food|Chilly Cooking]], or drinking [[Chilly Elixir]]s.<ref name="BotW Tips and Tricks"/> Both [[Gerudo Town]] and [[Kara Kara Bazaar]] provide constant protection from Heat.

The [[Rito]] traveler, [[Guy]], can be found in the Kara Kara Bazaar, waiting for the daytime Heat to pass in order to visit Gerudo Town.<ref name="BotW Guy"/> The [[Side Quest]] "[[An Ice Guy]]" involves giving a Chilly Elixir to Guy so that he can cross the Desert.<ref name="BotW Adventure Log"/>

==={{TotK|-}}===
{{Stub|TotK}}

==={{EoW|-}}===
The [[Gerudo Desert]] and its settlements, [[Gerudo Town]] and the [[Oasis]], are subject to intense Heat. Whenever [[Princess Zelda]] is idle in the Desert, she will begin to sweat and fan herself. However, she will not take damage as a result of the Heat.

==Other Appearances==
==={{HW|-}}===
{{Noncanon|Start}}
Desert Heat appears in the "[[Enduring Resolve]]" [[Scenario]]. Warriors caught within the Desert portion of [[Gerudo Desert (Stage)|Gerudo Desert]] will occasionally sustain minor damage from Desert Heat.<ref name="HW Lana"/> In order to curb the effects of the Desert Heat, the Hyrulean Forces must seize the North and South Oasis for the northern and southern portions of the Desert, respectively.<ref name="HW Lana 2"/><ref name="HW Battle Log 2"/>
{{Noncanon|End}}

